contributors (https://github.com/cipansor/crateworks).

The scores computed here reproduce those of fuzzywuzzy by SeatGeek and
contributors (https://github.com/seatgeek/fuzzywuzzy), which is distributed
under the MIT licence. The crate is an independent reimplementation in Rust and
shares no code with it; the upstream test suite was transcribed so that a
divergence from the reference shows up as a failing test. The algorithm itself
comes from CPython's difflib, which is distributed under the Python Software
Foundation Licence.

